      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "bug",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Dead selector: `.auth-links a + a` uses the adjacent-sibling combinator which only matches when two `\u003ca\u003e` elements are immediately adjacent. The login/signup templates wrap the two links with a `\u003cbr\u003e` between them (see `templates/login.html` lines 63–65), so the `margin-top: 0.5rem` rule never applies. Either remove the dead rule or rework the markup (e.g. remove the `\u003cbr\u003e` and rely on this rule, or change the selector to `.auth-links a:not(:first-child)` so it is robust to inter-element whitespace)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "static/auth.css"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 92,
                  "endLine": 92
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "ocrFinding/v1": "102ee69adb1b8624477f4ce5d001f660c0739bc44505c893248eea143c7479f8"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "static/auth.css"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 92,
                        "endLine": 92
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "/* Match any link that is not the first one, regardless of intervening elements */\n.auth-links a:not(:first-child) { display: inline-block; margin-top: 0.5rem; }"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "other",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Low-contrast trust-signal text: `rgba(255,255,255,0.35)` on the `--navy-900` (`#071B37`) background yields a contrast ratio around 3.5:1, which fails WCAG AA (4.5:1 required) for the small (~11px) uppercase text. Bump the opacity to at least `0.55`–`0.6` for the trust items, and consider raising the paragraph alpha (`0.55`) as well to be safe."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "static/auth.css"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 50,
                  "endLine": 54
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "ocrFinding/v1": "8969c80cbd30473575bcce4ec4be75327b53f8e85eef1510d638c303e9192ecb"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "static/auth.css"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 50,
                        "endLine": 54
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": ".auth-trust-item {\n  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.375rem;\n  font-size: 0.6875rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65); font-weight: 600;\n  text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em;\n}"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "maintainability",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Focus-icon rule is silently DOM-order-dependent: `.auth-input-group input:focus ~ .input-icon` only matches when the icon is a subsequent sibling of the input. It currently works because the templates place the `\u003csvg class=\"input-icon\"\u003e` after the `\u003cinput\u003e`, but any markup re-order (e.g. moving the icon before the input for source-order reasons) will silently kill the focus styling. Either add a defensive comment, or rewrite to a selector that is not order-dependent, e.g. `.auth-input-group:focus-within .input-icon { color: var(--brand); }`."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "static/auth.css"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 81,
                  "endLine": 81
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "ocrFinding/v1": "f1408c6b4b0d16dd123fb4d02e3f5decd5a5f7c17357c1d5dc55c1fa8aa8723e"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "static/auth.css"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 81,
                        "endLine": 81
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "/* `:focus-within` matches whenever any descendant is focused, so the rule\n   works regardless of whether the icon precedes or follows the input. */\n.auth-input-group:focus-within .input-icon { color: var(--brand); }"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "maintainability",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Implicit token coupling: this file relies on `--bg`, `--navy-900`, `--brand`, `--r-md`, `--font-display`, `--text-3`, `--text-4`, `--dur-fast` being defined elsewhere (in `static/style.css`). The stylesheet loads fine today, but if `style.css` is removed/renamed or tokens are renamed, the auth page degrades silently with no fallback values. Add a short comment at the top documenting the dependency, or include minimal `:root` fallback values for the most critical tokens (e.g. `--brand`, `--navy-900`, `--bg`) so the page degrades gracefully."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "static/auth.css"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1,
                  "endLine": 3
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "ocrFinding/v1": "c46f0c02e9b9ac9c1069355e906db25223846c972e68d065f8edbaad84a097fb"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "static/auth.css"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 1,
                        "endLine": 3
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "/* ============================================\n   Auth Pages — Bold split-screen\n   Depends on design tokens defined in static/style.css\n   (--bg, --navy-900, --brand, --r-md, --font-display,\n    --text-3, --text-4, --dur-fast). style.css must load\n   before this file.\n   ============================================ */"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "maintainability",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Responsive gap between breakpoints: only `900px` and `480px` are defined. Between `481px`–`899px` the brand panel collapses to full width but `.auth-trust-signals` still uses a horizontal row with `gap: 1.5rem`; on narrow tablets (e.g. ~500px wide) the row plus the SVG icons can overflow or wrap awkwardly. Consider stacking trust signals at a slightly higher threshold, or wrapping them with `flex-wrap: wrap` so they break gracefully on small tablets."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "static/auth.css"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 49,
                  "endLine": 49
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "ocrFinding/v1": "67cd7996675f288a24ea88c34d5b2ee69e437280bf2af8ac6922b7c8ea4c7805"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "static/auth.css"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 49,
                        "endLine": 49
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": ".auth-trust-signals { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 3rem; justify-content: center; }"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "maintainability",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "`.icon-copy-btn` is an interactive element (clipboard copy trigger) but has no `:focus-visible` (or `:focus`) styling. Keyboard-only users get no visible focus indicator, and the default browser outline is often suppressed in custom-themed apps. Add an explicit focus-visible state with a high-contrast outline/ring (e.g., `outline: 2px solid var(--brand); outline-offset: 2px;`) to satisfy WCAG 2.4.7."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "static/merchant.css"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 317,
                  "endLine": 325
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "ocrFinding/v1": "b8c51e633ecbe74d48e6c814c6850e3ed9d80972629d47751fca05627c73295d"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "static/merchant.css"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 317,
                        "endLine": 325
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": ".icon-copy-btn {\n  width: 38px;\n  height: 38px;\n  padding: 0;\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  background: var(--surface);\n  color: var(--text-2);\n  flex-shrink: 0;\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n\n.icon-copy-btn:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid var(--brand);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "maintainability",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "`.icon-copy-btn` sets fixed width/height and `padding: 0` but does not set `display: inline-flex` with center alignment. As a result the inline SVG (`display: inline`) is baseline-aligned and will sit slightly above/below the true vertical center of the 38×38 box across browsers. Add flex centering so the icon is reliably centered (and to satisfy the same selector in the suggestion above)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "static/merchant.css"
                },
