        {
          "ruleId": "bug",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The `.lime` class is miscolored — it uses `rgba(0,123,255,...)` blue background with `var(--brand)`, which is identical to the `.blue` class right below it. The file header explicitly advertises a \"Lime\" accent but no lime/yellow-green color is ever applied. Either rename `.lime` to `.blue` (and remove the redundant class), or change the background/color to an actual lime tone (e.g., `rgba(132,204,22,0.1)` + `#84CC16`). The dark-mode override on `.lime` (line below) is also distinct from `.blue`, suggesting `.lime` was originally intended to be a different color."
          },
          "locations": [
