          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "This stylesheet relies on many external custom properties that are never declared locally: `--surface`, `--surface-2`, `--text-1`, `--text-3`, `--brand`, `--brand-light`, `--border`, `--bg`, `--navy-900`, `--red`, `--shadow-md`, `--shadow-lg`, `--shadow-xl`, `--font-mono`, and `--admin-primary-dark`. If the global theme that provides them is missing, the rules silently fall back to `initial`, breaking the visual design with no console warning. Either redeclare these in the `:root` block here with safe defaults, or use `var(--name, fallback)` so each reference has an explicit fallback value."
