          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The selector `.admin-section[style*=\"display: none\"]` relies on matching a literal substring in the inline `style` attribute. Any future change in how sections are hidden (e.g. toggling a class, using `hidden` attribute, or `style.display = 'none '` with trailing whitespace) will silently break this rule. Also, since the element already has `display: none` inline, redeclaring `display: none` here is redundant. Replace with a dedicated utility class (e.g. `.is-hidden { display: none; }`) and toggle that class from JS."
