        {
          "ruleId": "performance",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Render-blocking external font import. CSS `@import` of Google Fonts blocks the render path, is serial (waits for parent stylesheet to parse), and competes with the rest of the stylesheet. Move the font URL out of CSS and load it via `\u003clink rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\"\u003e` + `\u003clink rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin\u003e` + `\u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"...\"\u003e` in the HTML head, and consider preloading the LCP-critical weight to avoid FOUT/CLS.\n\nAdditionally, the imported weights are over-specified: Plus Jakarta Sans requests 300/400/500/600/700/800 + italic 400, but the file only ever uses 700 (headings) and 400 (body); buttons use 600. Drop unused weights (300, 500, 800, the italic 400) to shrink the payload."
          },
