          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The theme toggle \u003cbutton\u003e has no `type` attribute, so it defaults to `type=\"submit\"`. It is not currently inside a \u003cform\u003e, but if one is ever added around `.legal-page` (e.g., a contact form per Section 8), clicking the toggle would submit that form. Set `type=\"button\"` explicitly. Also, the inline `onclick=\"toggleTheme()\"` and the inline `\u003cstyle\u003e` block both require `script-src 'unsafe-inline'` / `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` and will be blocked under a strict Content-Security-Policy. Prefer an addEventListener in a deferred external script and an external stylesheet so CSP can drop 'unsafe-inline'."
