          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored theme value is not validated. localStorage can be tampered with (extensions, shared device, scripted in console), so `localStorage.getItem('vb-theme')` could return any string. The CSS only defines `[data-theme=\"dark\"]`, so an arbitrary value silently degrades to the light cascade, which is harmless here, but the head script should still restrict to 'dark'/'light' so the attribute is never set to something unrenderable."
