          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Privacy policy content (Sections 1–4, 6, 7) explicitly states that user data is unprotected, freely shared, and accessible to anyone. This appears to be intentional dark humor for the VulnBank demo, but the template has no guard preventing it from being served to a real production build (no {% if config['DEMO'] %} wrapper, no banner, no environment check). If this codebase is ever deployed beyond an isolated demo, the page would be deceptive/misleading to actual users and would likely violate GDPR Art. 13/14, CCPA, and similar disclosure regimes. Recommend gating the route/template behind a demo-only flag or replacing the content with a real privacy policy before any non-demo release."
