          "message": {
            "text": "addLandingChatMessage concatenates an un-sanitized template into wrapper.innerHTML and relies on escapeLandingChatHtml() (only 5 entities). The escape is fine for the current text-node context, but the function is the only line of defense and uses innerHTML for everything. Any future change that moves the escaped value into an attribute or a JS string literal, or that adds an unescaped field to the template (e.g. AI response metadata, user display name, time format), silently re-introduces XSS. Prefer building the message node with createElement/textContent and setting .textContent on the message-text div so the escape function becomes unnecessary."
