          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The .lr class sets opacity:0 / translateY(24px) as the default state, and visibility is only restored by the IntersectionObserver in the inline \u003cscript\u003e. If JS is disabled, blocked, or fails (CSP, parse error in another script), all .lr sections including the hero h1/desc and the CTA remain permanently invisible — a serious progressive-enhancement regression. Either move the initial hidden state behind a .js .lr selector (so :root.no-js .lr shows content), or use a default-visible fallback that the script then hides before observing."
