          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "No CSRF protection on state-changing forms: `transferForm`, `loanForm`, `bioForm`, `profileUploadForm`, `createCardForm`, `fundCardForm`, and `payBillForm` have no visible CSRF token. Combined with cookie-based session auth this allows trivial cross-site request forgery on money-moving endpoints (transfers, loan requests, bill payments, card funding). Inject a CSRF token (Flask-WTF `{{ csrf_token() }}` or a hidden input) and validate it server-side, and require a custom header for fetch-based submissions so simple form POSTs are rejected."
