          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The form has neither an `action` nor a `method` attribute. If the JS submit handler (`merchant.js`) fails to load or throws before `e.preventDefault()`, the browser falls back to submitting a GET to the current URL, which appends card_number/cvv/expiry as query parameters — these then leak into browser history, server access logs, and the `Referer` header on outbound navigations (e.g., clicking \"API Docs\" or \"Personal App\" links). Add `action=\"/api/v1/payments/charge\" method=\"post\"` and `e.preventDefault()` so the fallback path never carries PAN/CVV."
          },
