          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Long-lived merchant secrets (API key and bearer JWT) are written into the DOM as plain text inside `\u003ccode\u003e` elements with copy-to-clipboard buttons. Anything that can read the rendered page — browser extensions, devtools, accidental screenshots, shoulder-surf, `view-source`, or a future XSS via the inline event handlers below — obtains credentials that authenticate against the merchant payment API. Consider: (a) gating reveal behind a re-auth step, (b) masking by default and only showing on a \"reveal\" action with auto-redaction after N seconds, (c) ensuring server-side values are HTML-escaped when populated, (d) not putting them in a copyable `\u003ccode\u003e` element where clipboard hijacking is trivial."
