          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Inline `onclick` handlers are used throughout the template (menu toggle, overlay, every nav link, logout, theme toggle, refresh, all copy buttons). This (a) prevents enabling a strict CSP with `script-src 'self'` and no `'unsafe-inline'`, (b) means any future interpolation of an untrusted value into one of these attributes is an immediate XSS sink (the JS is executed by the attribute parser without escaping), and (c) couples behavior to global function names that have to be hoisted by `merchant.js`. Wire these with `addEventListener` in merchant.js and use `data-` attributes (e.g., `data-action=\"toggle-sidebar\"`) when a parameter like an element ID is required."
          },
