          "message": {
            "text": "The pre-DOM theme bootstrap is an inline script in `\u003chead\u003e`, which forces any CSP to include `'unsafe-inline'` (or a per-request nonce/hash) and prevents auditing. The script itself reads `localStorage` from the parent context — fine here, but inline scripts are a known XSS amplification vector because they can't be reviewed at the same level as external files. Move this into `merchant.js` (or `vuln-disclaimer.js`) and either set the theme on a wrapping `\u003chtml class=\"loading\"\u003e` via a non-blocking external script, or render the `data-theme` attribute server-side from the persisted cookie so no client JS is needed."
