        {
          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing CSRF protection on registration form. The state-changing merchant-creation flow is submitted entirely from JS without a server-issued CSRF token (no hidden `_csrf_token` field, no `{{ csrf_token() }}`, no Flask-WTF `form.hidden_tag()`). When a strict `SameSite` cookie policy is not in place, this endpoint is vulnerable to cross-site request forgery — an attacker site can silently create merchant accounts on behalf of visitors. Add a CSRF token (e.g. Flask-WTF, itsdangerous-signed token, or a per-session token rendered into a hidden input that `merchant.js` forwards in the JSON body)."
