          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Password input lacks `autocomplete`, `minlength`, and there is no confirm-password field. `autocomplete=\"new-password\"` prevents password managers from autofilling a stored credential into a brand-new account (which would silently overwrite the user's intent) and signals account-creation semantics to the browser. `minlength` (and ideally a `pattern`) gives baseline client-side enforcement matching server-side policy. A confirm field prevents the common typo-then-account-locked-out support flow on a registration surface."
          },
