          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Inline `localStorage`-driven theme script runs before any CSP can apply and reads untrusted storage into the DOM. `setAttribute` itself is safe, but the inline-script pattern defeats `Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self'` (or forces `'unsafe-inline'`) and is the first thing to break when a nonce/hash-based CSP is later adopted. Move this into a static file (or use a nonce) so the page can ship a strict CSP that also blocks any future accidental `innerHTML` use against the same storage value."
