          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Suspend state desync bug: Jinja renders Python booleans as `True`/`False` (capitalised), but the JS compares `form.getAttribute('data-is-suspended') === 'true'` (lowercase). `isSuspended` is therefore always `false` on initial page load, regardless of the account's actual state. Combined with the toggle endpoint that flips state, after the first click the displayed \"Unsuspend/Suspend\" label drifts from reality for any account that started out suspended. Normalise the value to a lowercase string (`{{ 'true' if user[9] else 'false' }}`) or compare case-insensitively."
