          "ruleId": "maintainability",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Fragile positional indexing: the template indexes `user[0]..user[5]` and guards `user[9]` with `user|length \u003e 9`. Any reordering of the SQL `SELECT` (or a JOIN that changes column count) silently swaps usernames, account numbers, balances, roles and suspension state in the rendered table with no error surfaced. This is a security-relevant maintainability issue because the suspend button's correctness depends entirely on the wire shape staying identical. Refactor the route to pass a list of dicts (or a small dataclass) so the template binds by name."
