        {
          "ruleId": "bug",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unguarded localStorage access can throw and break page initialization. `localStorage.getItem(...)` throws a `SecurityError` in environments where storage is disabled (Safari private mode under certain configurations, sandboxed iframes, locked-down corporate browsers, or when third-party cookie/storage is blocked). When this throws, the `data-theme` attribute is never set, so the page renders without any theme applied and CSS variables may evaluate to undefined/initial values, producing a visually broken page. Wrap the read in a try/catch with a safe fallback so the page still renders correctly.\n\n```html\n\u003cscript\u003e\ntry {\n    document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\", localStorage.getItem(\"vb-theme\") || \"light\");\n} catch (e) {\n    document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\", \"light\");\n}\n\u003c/script\u003e\n```"
          },
