          "message": {
            "text": "`toggleTheme()` writes to localStorage without guarding for the same `SecurityError`. The attribute will still flip (so the UI works), but the call will throw and surface a console error on every click in restricted contexts, and the user's preference will not persist. Wrap the persistence in a try/catch so the toggle degrades gracefully.\n\n```html\n\u003cscript\u003e\n    function toggleTheme() {\n        const h = document.documentElement;\n        const n = h.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';\n        h.setAttribute('data-theme', n);\n        try { localStorage.setItem('vb-theme', n); } catch (e) {}\n    }\n\u003c/script\u003e\n```"
