          "message": {
            "text": "Inline `onclick` handler blocks a strict `Content-Security-Policy` (it requires `'unsafe-inline'`) and mixes concerns across the template. Although this is a demo app, the rest of the project will benefit from attaching the listener from a single, deferred script (matching the inline `\u003cscript\u003e` in `\u003chead\u003e` pattern already established here for the theme bootstrap). Consider:\n\n```html\n\u003cbutton class=\"theme-toggle\" id=\"theme-toggle\" aria-label=\"Toggle dark mode\" aria-pressed=\"false\"\u003e\n```\n\nwith a deferred script that wires it up via `addEventListener`. This also lets `unsafe-inline` be dropped from any future CSP and keeps markup clean."
