        {
          "ruleId": "other",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Theme toggle button lacks an `aria-pressed` state, so assistive-tech users get no indication of the current theme. The toggle is also a stateful control that toggles between two values; `role=\"switch\"` with `aria-checked` is the more semantically accurate pattern for a two-state toggle. Pair this with code that updates the attribute on every change so screen readers announce the new state.\n\n```html\n\u003cbutton class=\"theme-toggle\" id=\"theme-toggle\" type=\"button\" role=\"switch\" aria-label=\"Toggle dark mode\" aria-checked=\"false\"\u003e\n```"
