        {
          "ruleId": "bug",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "All fetch handlers branch on `data.status` without checking `response.ok` (or even `response.status`) before `response.json()`. On non-2xx responses with empty/non-JSON bodies (e.g. 502 from a proxy, 429 with plain text) `response.json()` throws and the user only sees the generic catch message (\"Merchant registration failed\", \"Could not load payments\", etc.), masking real server errors and rate-limit signals. Add `if (!response.ok) { ... }` before parsing, surface `response.status` in the message, and only fall through to `data.status` after confirming success."
          },
