          "ruleId": "bug",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Success-message can be immediately overwritten by a follow-up failure. After a successful charge the code calls `await fetchMerchantPayments()`; if that throws or returns non-success, fetchMerchantPayments itself calls showMerchantMessage('Could not load payments'), clobbering the \"Payment approved\" success state the user just saw. Either keep the success message sticky until the user dismisses / reloads, or only show the failure as a non-blocking warning. Also note the concurrent refreshMerchantProfile fired by loadMerchantDashboard can race with this and reorder UI updates — sequence or guard against overlapping fetches."
