          "ruleId": "maintainability",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The 300ms in setTimeout(() =\u003e sheet.remove(), 300) is a magic number duplicated from the CSS transition-duration. If the transition is tuned in the stylesheet (or prefers-reduced-motion overrides it), the node is removed before (or after) the animation completes, producing a visible jump or an orphaned backdrop. Either read the duration from the computed style, listen for transitionend, or store the value as a CSS variable and read it from JS."
