        {
          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "/api/transfer has multiple compounding defects: (1) TOCTOU race — SELECT balance then two separate UPDATEs are not atomic, so under Flask's threaded server two concurrent transfers can both pass the \u003e= amount check and overdraw the account; wrap the read+write in a single transaction (BEGIN IMMEDIATE) or use a conditional UPDATE that enforces the balance invariant atomically. (2) SQL injection in `id={current_user['user_id']}`, `amount={amount}`, and `account_number='{to_account}'` — all must be parameterized. (3) current_user['user_id'] is never validated as the owner of the debited row, so a token's user_id (which the client can attempt to influence via the JWT claims) is trusted blindly. (4) `amount` is not validated — it can be negative, NaN, infinity, or a string cast failure, enabling fund theft and crashes."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
