        {
          "ruleId": "bug",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Transfer accepts negative amounts and uses `abs(amount)` for the funds check, while the UPDATEs apply the signed value. With amount=-N the sender passes the check (balance \u003e= |N|), the debit becomes `balance - (-N) = balance + N` (sender is credited) and the recipient loses N. This permits stealing funds from arbitrary accounts and creating money. Reject negative amounts and check `amount \u003e 0 and balance \u003e= amount`."
          },
