            "text": "`_install_fake_psycopg2` mutates `sys.modules` in `setUpClass` with no `tearDownClass` to restore the originals, so the fake persists for every subsequent test file imported into the same process. Combined with the early-return guard `if \"psycopg2\" in sys.modules: return`, two problems appear: (a) test ordering now determines whether this file installs its stub or silently inherits a real psycopg2 imported earlier, and (b) other test modules that legitimately need real psycopg2 will see the stub. The fakes should be torn down after the class runs, or installed only on the import path of the SUT without polluting `sys.modules`."
