          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "`pg_isready -d ${DB_NAME}` requires the database to already exist; on a brand-new PostgreSQL instance it will return errors like \"FATAL: database ... does not exist\" rather than just \"not accepting connections\", which masks the real readiness signal and can interact badly with the unbounded retry loop. Probe server readiness first, then ensure the database exists (CREATE DATABASE if missing) before the loop, or drop the `-d` flag and rely on a separate `psql` check for DB existence."
