          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "`docker compose down` before `up -d --build` causes full downtime between the old and new containers. Use `docker compose up -d --build --remove-orphans` (which performs a rolling recreate) or an explicit blue/green / health-gated rollout. Also be aware that `set -e` plus `docker compose down` means a failure here aborts the deploy but leaves the old stack already torn down — there is no rollback."
          },
