          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "`rsync --delete` combined with `--exclude '.env'` is fragile: depending on rsync version/flag order, excluded files can still be deleted on the receiving side, which would wipe `/home/.../vuln-bank/.env` on every deploy and trigger the `cp .env.example .env` bootstrap below — overwriting production secrets with example/insecure defaults on each run. Use `--filter='P .env'` (protect) or `--filter='protect .env'` so the file is both excluded from transfer and protected from deletion, and ship real secrets via a separate secret-injection mechanism (not via `cp .env.example .env`)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ".github/workflows/deploy.yml"
