          "ruleId": "security",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The `match` field stores the full detected high-entropy string in plaintext. This makes the cache file itself a secrets leak: if `.cache_ggshield` is ever committed to VCS, copied into a backup, attached to a CI artifact, or written into a shared home directory, the very credential ggshield is trying to protect is exposed. The cache should store only a non-reversible fingerprint (e.g., SHA-256 of the match + file + commit) and keep the raw secret out of disk. At a minimum the file must be in `.gitignore` and excluded from any artifact upload paths."
          },
          "locations": [
