          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "No allow-list / dismissed / reviewed flag. The matched value is a 64-char hex string inside a test file (`tests/test_merchant_payments.py`), almost certainly a SHA-256 hash fixture rather than a real credential. Without an explicit `status` (e.g., `\"new\"`, `\"ignored\"`, `\"acknowledged\"`) or an allow-list key, ggshield will permanently suppress this detection on every subsequent run while still reporting it as a live secret, which both hides real future leaks in the same file and floods the user with an un-actionable warning."
