            "text": "HEALTHCHECK concerns: (1) It relies on a `/healthz` endpoint whose existence and 200 behavior is not enforced by the Dockerfile — if the app is misconfigured the check may always fail or always pass depending on routing. (2) `start-period=30s` is often too short for apps that do DB migrations, load ML models, or warm caches — a healthy container may be killed/looped during cold start. (3) The inline `urllib.request.urlopen` call swallows many error classes via Python exception; the shell will only see a non-zero exit if the Python process crashes, which is OK but consider a dedicated `curl` or `wget` one-liner that returns proper HTTP status. (4) No `HEALTHCHECK CMD` fallback if `python` is unavailable in PATH after USER switch."
